$NetBSD$

Use the correct encoding-specific ID3 APIs and portable iconv names.
The payload is selected by TextEncoding: UTF-8 APIs take char strings and
UTF-16 APIs take unsigned short strings. Do not suppress GCC diagnostics.
UTF destinations do not need GNU //TRANSLIT, rejected by Citrus iconv.
Retain GNU Latin-1 transliteration where available, with a standard fallback.
The generic UTF-8 field must call the UTF-8 API, not the Latin-1 setter.
Origin: EmberBSD; AI-assisted portability fix, not submitted upstream.

